perl-IO-Tee: perl-IO-Tee (multiplex output to multiple filehandles)
perl-IO-Tee:
perl-IO-Tee: IO::Tee lets a Perl program send what it prints to several
perl-IO-Tee: filehandles at once. It returns a tied handle: anything written
perl-IO-Tee: to it is copied to every handle given to the constructor, such as
perl-IO-Tee: STDOUT and a log file. It can also read from a first input handle
perl-IO-Tee: and copy the data it reads to the other handles.
